From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: apklayer <apklayer@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] ShadowAlarmManager: PendingIntent alarms go to a hook (the instance hub holds them)

apklayer patch: with auto scheduling a PendingIntent alarm is handed to PendingAlarms.hook (runtime/patches; the hub's HostAlarms, HubScheduler keeps it, so it fires
after the app process is gone, as AlarmManagerService does) instead of the process-local Handler; deschedule tells the hook to cancel.

Against external/robolectric 87aa52b08 (REVISION), after 0009. Applied by scripts/build-runtime-overlay.sh onto the staged
upstream sources; the result is compiled into native-runtime.jar ahead of Robolectric_all.jar.
---
diff --git a/shadows/framework/src/main/java/org/robolectric/shadows/ShadowAlarmManager.java b/shadows/framework/src/main/java/org/robolectric/shadows/ShadowAlarmManager.java
index fef54bc..4f1cd1b 100644
--- a/shadows/framework/src/main/java/org/robolectric/shadows/ShadowAlarmManager.java
+++ b/shadows/framework/src/main/java/org/robolectric/shadows/ShadowAlarmManager.java
@@ -705,12 +705,17 @@ public class ShadowAlarmManager {
       if (autoSchedule) {
         // apklayer patch: an RTC alarm's time is a wall-clock time, not elapsed realtime (its delay was years, it never fired)
         long now = type == AlarmManager.RTC || type == AlarmManager.RTC_WAKEUP ? System.currentTimeMillis() : SystemClock.elapsedRealtime();
+        // apklayer patch: a PendingIntent alarm is held by the hub (outlives the process), which sends it when due
+        if (operation != null && PendingAlarms.hook != null && PendingAlarms.hook.set(operation, triggerAtTime - now, interval)) {
+          return this;
+        }
         schedulingHandler.postDelayed(this, triggerAtTime - now);
       }
       return this;
     }
 
     void deschedule() {
+      if (autoSchedule && operation != null && PendingAlarms.hook != null) PendingAlarms.hook.cancel(operation);  // apklayer patch
       schedulingHandler.removeCallbacks(this);
     }
 
